          "Input volumes 25+75 give 25%; scaling 10+30 still 25%; 20+30 gives 40%. For ethanol 40 mL + water 60 mL before mixing, contracted final 96 mL leaves the defined input-volume fraction 40%; 40/96=41.6667% is a different ratio. No separate 40 mL region is inferred inside the homogeneous mixture. Fresh transfer supplies A=20 mL and final=40 mL with B unknown: no justified fraction until B input is requested; supplied B=30 mL under equal conditions gives 40%. This changes information structure/reference reasoning rather than just numbers."
